==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Makoto Shishio CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Makoto Shishio is a bona-fide bruiser with solid all-around stats. His main selling point is the sheer scaling of the numbers he brings to the table: 14,535 DPS against targets at Lv.30 (23,085 at Lv.50) with a 100% [[Strengthen]] at 30% HP bringing his output to 32,300 (51,300) accounting for his [[Cat Combo]]. This isn't mentioning the fact that he has 488,750 effective HP against targets through [[Strong Against]] (776,250 at level 50). These stats aren't anything to sneeze at, and he does well enough to absolutely obliterate many stages via complete stat-stomp, but he comes with various caveats. For one, he only has one knockback, so no repositioning whatsoever outside of enemy abilities. Even with his gargantuan health pool, it only takes one unfortunate series of events to send him back to the bleachers. To make matters worse, he stays contemplating his terrible life choices for almost 6 minutes before recharging. Treat him like a [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Nekoluga]] in that sense; you only get one shot with him, so you better make it count. You'll also want to keep enemies a good distance away from him at all times, since his output drops considerably at close quarters because of how [[Explosion]] operates. [[Slow]] helps him with that, but it's unreliable at the best of times and he desperately needs the supplemental support from other cats to shake off tankier enemies like [[Cyberhorn]] and [[St. Dober]].

With all of that said, he can easily be worth the hassle, as the solution to many seemingly complex stages can be to  simply outstat the main threats. Such is apparent in stages like [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]], [[Banana Genomes]], [[Beyond the Hadal]], and so forth. He holds his own very well in ideal circumstances, and the Angel/Alien combo is surprisingly common from [[Into the Future]] and onwards. [[Wave Immunity]] is also a very nice add-on that lets him work better against [[Youcan]] and [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] amongst other common untargeted Wavers like [[Pigeon de Sable]], though [[Explosion Immunity]] is only really good for [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]]' Brutal Advent stages. As a result, he has decently good viability across the board.

